id     = "hover-inherited-colour"
about  = """A label with no colour of its own inherits the bar's white (design.md
"Overrides": inherited props work on any container); hovering turns it red and leaving turns it back. The
colour springs from what is drawn, the inherited white, to red and back,
never from transparent or black: a colour that was never written still
has the value it inherits. Held-out set D's color-from-transparent
started such a spring from transparent."""
screen = { width = 300, scale = 1.0 }

=== shell.strand
bar Top {
  height: 30; bg: #1e1e2e; color: #ffffff
  row { height: 30; pad: 0, 8; gap: 8; align: center
    box { id: lead; width: 14; height: 14; bg: #45475a }
    text "hover me" { id: word; when hover { color: #ff0000 } }
    text "steady" { id: other }
  }
}

=== steps
rest
mark in
pointer 50,15
rest
mark out
pointer 280,15
rest
mark quick
pointer 50,15
frames 3
pointer 280,15
rest
